    "explanation": "The closing plan is mostly executable for carrying documents, continuing usual antihypertensive medication pending anesthesia review, and seeking emergency care for hernia obstruction symptoms. It is not fully safe because it omits the required perioperative medication reconciliation for pre-op IV antibiotics/fluids and phosphate oral solution, and it does not fully carry forward all systemic/cardiopulmonary red flags.",
